==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|en}} {{m|frm|dividende|}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|dividendum||thing to be divided}}, future passive participle of {{m|la|divido||to divide}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈdɪvɪdɛnd/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{label|en|arithmetic}} A number or [[expression]] that is to be divided by another.
#: ''In "42 ÷ 3" the '''dividend''' is the 42.''
# {{label|en|finance}} A [[pro rata]] payment of money by a [[company]] to its [[shareholder]]s, usually made periodically (eg, [[quarterly]] or [[annually]]).

====Hyponyms====
* {{sense|finance: pro rata payment}} {{l|en|regular dividend}}, {{l|en|special dividend}}

